.TH GETENV 3
.SH NAME
getenv \- value for environment name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "char *getenv(name)"
.B "char *name;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getenv
searches the environment list (see
.BR environ (5))
for a string of the
form
.IR name = value
and returns
.I value
if such a string is present, otherwise
0 (NULL).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
environ(5), exec(2)
.sp
